                            <comment id="497516" author="JIRAUSER19474" created="Wed, 8 Jul 2026 21:18:11 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Code Analysis&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In `lustre/ldlm/ldlm_flock.c`, the lock split code path:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;if (new2 == NULL) {&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    unlock_res_and_lock(req);           // Release lock for allocation&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    new2 = ldlm_lock_create(...);       // May fail with -ENOMEM&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    lock_res_and_lock(req);             // Re-acquire lock&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    if (IS_ERR(new2)) &lt;/p&gt;
{

        ldlm_flock_destroy(req, lock-&amp;gt;l_granted_mode, *flags);

        *err = PTR_ERR(new2);

        RETURN(LDLM_ITER_STOP);         // BUG: Returns with lock held!

    }

&lt;p&gt;    goto reprocess;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;}&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This occurs when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. A process holds a byte-range flock (e.g., bytes 0-999)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. It unlocks a middle portion (e.g., bytes 100-199)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;3. Server needs to split the lock into two separate locks&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;4. `ldlm_lock_create()` fails due to memory pressure (-ENOMEM)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;5. Error path returns without releasing the resource lock&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
